            {
                "entry_id": "fbb44ec0-fd16-3040-9070-20b8410b7b16",
                "word": "ми",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b61d50e-97cd-3fcf-921c-17cca9ddb8c2",
                        "entry_id": "fbb44ec0-fd16-3040-9070-20b8410b7b16",
                        "glosses": [
                            "лингв. новогреческое название буквы мю"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62fe759b-595f-45f4-973e-63b438919160",
                        "source_entry_id": "fbb44ec0-fd16-3040-9070-20b8410b7b16",
                        "source_sense_id": "7b61d50e-97cd-3fcf-921c-17cca9ddb8c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "mu",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mu",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc630bfc-6505-3a14-8ee5-328e2726827f",
                                        "entry_id": "cde6f3dc-e737-3b9e-afe2-2ebe6918e320",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The 12th letter of the Modern Greek alphabet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mu",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42e07123-b8cb-372d-a636-e986177b6f31",
                                        "entry_id": "f482c360-33e4-3c0b-8938-03983dc58bae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Neither yes nor no."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75b3a2db-e2f4-4f3f-b9b0-4e84834b9e0c",
                                                "sense_id": "42e07123-b8cb-372d-a636-e986177b6f31",
                                                "text": "Mu means \"no thing.\" Like \"Quality\" it points outside the process of dualistic discrimination. Mu simply says, \"No class; not one, not zero, not yes, not no.\" […] It's a great mistake, a kind of dishonesty, to sweep nature's mu answers under the carpet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4c65d6f-8c3f-4462-84e1-5c45fad1f135",
                                                "sense_id": "42e07123-b8cb-372d-a636-e986177b6f31",
                                                "text": "Achilles: Oh, but MU is Jōshū’s answer. By saying MU, Jōshū let the other monk know that only by not asking such questions can one know the answer to them.\nTortoise: Jōshū “unasked” the question. […]\nAchilles: […] And the answer of “MU” here rejects the premises of the question, which are that one or the other must be chosen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01aacca6-a1f2-45ac-842f-4243fb3ccb5d",
                                                "sense_id": "42e07123-b8cb-372d-a636-e986177b6f31",
                                                "text": "\"Mu,\" said Kelly Dahl.\nOn one level mu means only yes, but on a deeper level of Zen it was often used by the master when the acolyte asked a stupid, unanswerable or wrongheaded question such as \"Does a dog have the Buddha-nature?\" The Master would answer only, \"Mu,\" meaning—I say \"yes\" but mean \"no,\" but the actual answer is: Unask the question."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35931e6c-f48d-4c66-b21f-7f6548b41b9a",
                                                "sense_id": "42e07123-b8cb-372d-a636-e986177b6f31",
                                                "text": "The Fifth Patriarch's utterance You say mu [Buddha-nature] because Buddha-nature is emptiness articulates clearly and distinctly the truth that emptiness is not \"no\". In uttering Buddha-nature-emptiness one does not say \"half a pound.\" One does not say \"eight ounces.\" One says \"mu.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6bd4386-2759-446e-87b9-11e6cbf9bd2c",
                                                "sense_id": "42e07123-b8cb-372d-a636-e986177b6f31",
                                                "text": "A monk once asked Master Joshu, 'Has a dog the Buddha Nature or not?' Joshu said, 'Mu!'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mu",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45b3da6a-c0d8-3b38-8a0f-2c210412e65e",
                                        "entry_id": "a83af819-16f7-3750-8a2d-879c12757c7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nothingness; nonexistence; the illusory nature of reality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "447e6b69-31ef-4ad1-a6f9-09daf5a57f34",
                                                "sense_id": "45b3da6a-c0d8-3b38-8a0f-2c210412e65e",
                                                "text": "That being the case, we should naturally choose to contemplate mu from morning to night, forgetting everything."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc9a5427-a4ba-4fc0-951e-3479636cabc7",
                                                "sense_id": "45b3da6a-c0d8-3b38-8a0f-2c210412e65e",
                                                "text": "Consequently, though mu is mindlike, the likeness to individual consciousness cannot be pushed very far."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27fe1161-a6b2-4cc6-b82d-adc5d3f9f3ca",
                                                "sense_id": "45b3da6a-c0d8-3b38-8a0f-2c210412e65e",
                                                "text": "The monk posed to Chaoi-chou a question: Does a dog have a buddha nature or not?\" Chao-chou, without a moment's hesitation, answered, “Mu.\" (Translated as \"No.\")"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f565e470-8565-4006-aac4-d7161c9d8beb",
                                                "sense_id": "45b3da6a-c0d8-3b38-8a0f-2c210412e65e",
                                                "text": "If mu is mind, consciousness, it is nothing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mu",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2aa228a8-96d9-3c63-9b01-b9e0d1caa3b4",
                                        "entry_id": "7600bb14-7500-312c-8b21-682b88f719ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A unit of surface area, currently equivalent to two-thirtieths of a hectare."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5cb0343-2bcb-48a8-9cfe-852c13b91812",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa228a8-96d9-3c63-9b01-b9e0d1caa3b4",
                                                "text": "The Lucky Star Co-operative in Chuwo County on the plains of southern Shansi had, before the anti-Japanese war, 26 wells, 4 water-wheels and 166.1 mou of irrigated fields, 4.82 per cent of its total arable land.",
                                                "translation": "中国农业合作化的道路",
                                                "english": "中国农业合作化的道路"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "344649a4-8cb8-466a-a836-8ef15b47e58f",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa228a8-96d9-3c63-9b01-b9e0d1caa3b4",
                                                "text": "Good news on the summer harvest prevailed in the countryside of Chienchiang County, Hupeh. The county reported remarkable increased in its 600,000 mou of summer food crops this year, surpassing the yield in 1962 which was considered as the best year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a236ed9-3cdf-475c-8c5f-514392be8f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa228a8-96d9-3c63-9b01-b9e0d1caa3b4",
                                                "text": "Pengyang county was administered by Guyuan before 1988. In contrast to Guyuan, Pengyang is relatively wealthy. Farmers earn a considerable income through tobacco cultivation, which can yield an annual gross income of Rmb 1,500-2,000 per mu. In 1996, the cultivated area of tobacco in Pengyang was 11,000 mu.⁷"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf715b9b-d224-41e3-860e-e1043f302033",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa228a8-96d9-3c63-9b01-b9e0d1caa3b4",
                                                "text": "Of 114 village farming families, only ten had more than 30 mu of land and only five had more than 60 mu."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
